## Project Overview

### Phase 1
PHASE 1: SETUP (30 min)

Create folder structure: /linkedin-to-resume ├── backend └── frontend

Backend setup:

Initialize with npm init -y

Install dependencies: express, cors, playwright, typescript, ts-node

Create server.ts with:

CORS

Port: 3001

Frontend setup:

Create React app (CRA with TypeScript)

Install @tanstack/react-query if using React Query

Build simple form UI

Confirm:

Both backend and frontend run

Frontend successfully fetches /api/ping

✅ Checkpoint 1: Project is live end-to-end

## Phase 2
PHASE 2: BASIC SCRAPER MVP (1 hour)

In backend /api/scrape?url=...:

Launch Playwright

Set User-Agent

Navigate to LinkedIn URL

Scrape:

Name (e.g., from <h1>)

Profile Picture URL (first reasonable <img>)

Return minimal JSON: { "name": "Jane Doe", "photoUrl": "https://..." }

Frontend:

Submit URL, fetch data

Display name and image

Show loading/error states

✅ Checkpoint 2: Input LinkedIn URL → see name & photo

## Phase 3
PHASE 3: EXPAND SCRAPING (1 hour)

Scrape Work Experience:

Anchor to "Experience" heading

Extract: title, company, dateRange, description (if possible)

Scrape Education:

Anchor to "Education"

Extract: degree, school, dateRange

Update API JSON: { "name": "...", "photoUrl": "...", "workExperience": [{ title, company, dateRange, description }], "education": [{ degree, school, dateRange }] }

✅ Checkpoint 3: Full profile data returned from backend

## Phase 4
PHASE 4: PDF RESUME WITH REACT-PDF (1–1.5 hours)

Install @react-pdf/renderer

Build ResumeDocument.tsx:

Use <Document> + <Page wrap>

Add fixed <View> for header and footer

Layout:

Profile Picture

Name

Work Experience

Education

Use <PDFDownloadLink> to generate download button

✅ Checkpoint 4: Resume PDF rendered from real profile data

## Phase 5
PHASE 5: POLISH & DELIVERY (30–45 min)

Frontend:

Loading spinner during fetch

Error message on failure

Write README:

Tech stack

How to run

Assumptions / tradeoffs

Known issues

Future improvements

Git: git add . git commit -m "Final working version" git push origin main

✅ Final Checkpoint: MVP complete, PDF clean, repo pushable
